66	  // ── Kill switch ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
67	  // Placed after the project lookup (so an unknown project still 404s, and the
68	  // switch never leaks the existence of someone else's project) and before
69	  // EVERY spend path below it: the balance read, the spend cap, the Build row,
70	  // the user Message row and the model call in runAgent. Refusing here writes
71	  // nothing at all and charges nothing at all.
72	  //
73	  // Its own status and its own words, deliberately. The two checks immediately
74	  // below both answer 402 and both talk about credits; reusing either would
75	  // tell the user they are out of money during an incident that has nothing to
76	  // do with their balance, and they would go and top up. 503 is the honest
77	  // code: the capability is temporarily withdrawn by us.
78	  //
79	  // Bucketed on user.id — stable per user, so a partial rollout (if this were
80	  // ever operated as one) cannot flip the same person between requests.
