333	/* The prompt-box glow ring (PromptHero) — a Gemini-style "chasing light"
334	   ring, rebuilt using only decade-old, maximally-compatible CSS: plain
335	   `transform: rotate()` and `overflow: hidden` clipping. No @property, no
336	   CSS masking — both were dropped after repeated reports that the effect
337	   still wasn't appearing correctly even in a fresh browser with a verified
338	   non-cached, up-to-date stylesheet, which means the earlier @property +
339	   mask-composite combination (both comparatively modern CSS features) was
340	   the most likely remaining suspect, even though I could not get direct
341	   visual confirmation either way in this environment.
342	
343	   The technique: each layer is a STATIC outer clipper
344	   (`.glow-clip-a/-b`, position:absolute, overflow:hidden, never
345	   transforms) containing one OVERSIZED inner rotator
346	   (`.glow-spin-a/-b`, ~2x the clipper's size, centered via inset:-50%).
347	   Only the inner rotator spins via plain `transform: rotate()` — since
348	   it's oversized, its corners sweeping outside a same-sized box (the
349	   original "wide rectangle rotated as a rigid body" bug) never matters:
350	   they're clipped away by the static outer box at every angle. The
351	   composer sitting on top (z-10, opaque) covers the rotator's entire
352	   interior, leaving only the outer few px visible as a ring — no masking
